Z||000000||SloPonti||01-12-2001||12:16 AM||||i see there are two different major companies to get lowering springs from! eibachs are about 1 drop and suspension techs is about 1.5 inches and cheaper! what is the difference-better springs or a name thing? any help would be great!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob  <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/sloponti/fiero1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||01-12-2001||08:49 AM||||I've installed both (eibachs on my SE and STs on BlackGTs car)the STs look nicer the Eibachs still leave a pretty big fender gap. there isn't much of a ride difference.. the Shock valving controls how harsh the ride is. i had Konis and turned full open was WAY squisher than Todds Sensa trac/ST setup. i'd say the STs...  part number 60210. <A HREF="http://www.cyberauto.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cyberauto.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.shox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.shox.com</A>  and bilstiens or KYBs... the Konis are nice but a pain to tune... ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ferg||01-12-2001||09:11 AM||||1fst- did you notice any adverse handling charateristics after the spring mod? Was the ride much rougher than stock? Did the suspension work as well as in stock form? <P>Reason I asked was, I've had a lowered pickup before, and I always read that you had to replace the spindle to keep the suspension geometry the same. Does this not matter when you're dealing w/ only a couple of inches. (The drops I'm used to are 3-5 inches in the front and 5-7 inches in the rear)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||01-12-2001||10:08 AM||||travis... does bilstein make shocks/struts for the fiero?  if so, i wish i had know 2 months ago.  i would've much rather had those than the KYB's (not to diss kyb, they are nice strut's)<P>i have poly bushings, kybs and eibach springs.  the ride is really not that bad (these are sportscars, afterall)... sometimes it gets a bit bouncy on lumpy roads.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||5
Z||000004||KEV||01-12-2001||01:35 PM||||hay bhooper bilstin quite making shocks & struts for the fiero a long time ago but sachs/boge they are standered equip. on many german cars and they would be very equal to the bilstins and koni. I'm planning on goin to sachs on my 85GT 3800V6 after i take it out of storage.<p>[This message has been edited by KEV (edited 01-12-2001).]||||reg||1
