Z||000012||Sleeper||01-13-2001||10:56 AM||||For those of you that wanna know...INTRAX makes lowering springs for all makes and model Fieros and YES they are a great company. They lower the car 1.8 in the front and 1.7 in the rear. You can buy them direct from intrax at <A HREF="http://www.intraxsuspension.com" TARGET=_blank>www.intraxsuspension.com</A>  for $299 or you can buy them from summit <A HREF="http://www.summitracing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.summitracing.com</A>  for just $209.<P>Opps, part# for these a summit is int-25-1-020<p>[This message has been edited by Sleeper (edited 01-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||SloPonti||01-15-2001||12:27 AM||||i have never heard of intraxx! does anyone have these springs on there car? how are they compared to eibachs and suspension tech? thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000014||1FST2M6||01-15-2001||11:32 AM||||intrax are fine springs... the ride didn't change at all on Todds car.. since he went from stock w/sensa-trac to lower w/sensa-tracs.. it's just .. yep.. lower... my koni SE was a PAIN in the butt! took about 2 weeks to dial them in right... then it handled great but shook/broke your teeth... bilstein stoped making them in 95 but AutoDelta has a couple sets left.. i'll get a real price and part numbers and let you all know... (AutoDelta is the new warehousing importer for Alfa Romeo and Mackin industries) they have some stuff warehoused all over.. i was fortunate to know todd Spruell of Paul Spruell Alfa, Lambo, Lotus and get a set cheap... i'll get pics for ya to drool over..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">    i have custom wound springs so my car rides like $h!t on a stick but it handles great and is great on the highway. but bumpy country roads upset it. ||||reg||1
Z||000015||batboy||01-15-2001||03:56 PM||||I have the S/T springs on the front of the Batmobile. Good springs, cheaper and about 1/2" lower than the Eibachs. Never hits the bump stops (but I do have a V8 in the rear). But, they are not variable spring rate lowering springs like the Eibachs. Weekend warriors and those on a tight budget will be happy with S/T springs. Fussy folks into handling will prefer the Eibachs. If you ever plan on racing, go with coil-over kits.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/batkid3.gif">   <B>BATBOY</B><BR>1985 SE auto with 350 Chevy V8 (Batmobile),<BR>suspension mods, lowered, GA brakes, etc...||||reg||1
